  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F9A77E">Definition <span data-tag="F9A77E">4.3.2.2</span>.</a> Suppose given a commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \calC ^{0} \ar @{^{(}->}[d] \ar [r]^{F_0} &amp;  \calD \ar [d]^{p} \\ \calC \ar [r] \ar [ur]^{F} &amp;  \calD ', } \]
</div>
  <p> where $p$ is an inner fibration and the left vertical map is the inclusion of a full subcategory $\calC ^{0} \subseteq \calC $. </p>
  <p>We will say that $F$ is a <em>$p$-left Kan extension of $F_0$ at $C \in \calC $</em> if the induced diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { (\calC ^{0}_{/C}) \ar @{^{(}->}[d] \ar [r]^{F_ C} &amp;  \calD \ar [d]^{p} \\ (\calC _{/C}^{0})^{\triangleright } \ar [ur] \ar [r] &amp;  \calD ' } \]
</div>
  <p> exhibits $F(C)$ as a $p$-colimit of $F_{C}$. </p>
  <p>We will say that $F$ is a <em>$p$-left Kan extension of $F_0$</em> if it is a $p$-left Kan extension of $F_0$ at $C$, for every object $C \in \calC $. </p>
  <p>In the case where $\calD ' = \Delta ^0$, we will omit mention of $p$ simply say that $F$ is a <em>left Kan extension of $F_0$</em> if the above condition is satisfied.Kan extension </p>
